    "updated_at": "2016-09-13T14:14:40Z",
    "body": "_Sigh_.  I don't know what you searched, exactly, but...\n\nThe original fix was in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=371360 and the obvious followup with \"oh, that broke things\" was https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=409888.  In particular, see discussion starting at https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=371360#c53 and going through comment 65 and see https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=401611.\n\nI don't have time to page all this in again right now, but a brief skim suggests that there were two failure modes:\n1.  Pages doing a form submit inside the unload handler and suddenly not having their data submitted.\n2.  Pages doing a location.replace in the unload handler to provide users with a better session history experience (because they had some sort of interstitial page stuff going on for other reasons).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
