    "created_at": "2016-09-13T20:44:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-13T20:44:59Z",
    "body": "Thanks very much for your help. It is interesting that those pages have not reported any compatibility issues with IE/Edge/Safari. Maybe we will see them when Chrome's new behavior hits stable (cc @lucasgadani).\n\nAs for the specific cases in those bugs:\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=401611#c0 the mentioned website (http://www.cloverlick.com/) no longer seems to exist\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=401611#c28 still works since it is navigating a new browsing context, not the current one.\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=371360#c78 the mentioned page (https://www.workday.com/resources/whitepapers/whitepaper_form.php) no longer seems to exist.\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=372666#c18 the mentioned page (https://www.cs.helsinki.fi/u/pettay/moztests/unload_change_location.html) is now 403ing.\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=257874 behaves the same in all browsers, I guess because all browsers consider javascript URLs to be different-origin. Same for https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=257952\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=247660#c0 the mentioned site (karstenw.customer.netspace.net.au) no longer seems to exist.\n- https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=247660#c0 the test case given as text, copied to a local server (https://ns-ivkhryvhyf.now.sh), behaves differently in Edge/Chrome Canary/Chrome Stable/Safari (per this spec patch) vs. giving a 404 in Firefox (per the current spec... I think)\n\nI also tested the test case from the OP in Safari Tech Preview and Safari stable, and got that it passes (i.e. aligns with Chrome Canary and Edge).\n\nMy conclusion from all of this investigation is that we should probably align with the 3/4 behavior of disallowing all such navigations, i.e. merge this pull request. I'm happy to write and submit the web platform tests, as well as file a Gecko bug.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
